            0.593,
            0.127
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "The Journey Beyond"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.162,
            0.774,
            0.214
          ],
          "content": "y Create an ‘Atomic Prediction Board’ game based on atomic number, mass number, number of electrons, protons, neutrons and valency. Students may predict elements using atomic clues."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.217,
            0.774,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "y Prepare a report on how the properties of atoms impact us in everyday life across fields, such as healthcare, energy, agriculture and technology."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.27,
            0.773,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "y Create a role-play, stage play or story about the ‘Journey Inside the Atom’, and the scientists who discovered and contributed to the identification of atomic structure."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.325,
            0.774,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": "y Use selected software or digital tools and try to create animations or simulations of various atomic models, and share them in the class."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.362,
            0.774,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": "y Watch a film or documentary about the structure of the atom and write a report answering the following questions:"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.778,
            0.137,
            0.924,
            0.409
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_21_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.4,
            0.774,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": " Which film or documentary did you watch, and what was its main idea or topic?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.437,
            0.775,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": " What did the film or documentary teach you about the structure of the atom and the atomic model(s)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.474,
            0.773,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": " Which scientists were mentioned in the film or documentary, and what were their contributions?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.511,
            0.773,
            0.547
          ],
          "content": " What part of the film or documentary did you find most interesting, and what question do you still have?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.549,
            0.774,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": "y Draw a bar graph showing the number of electrons in each energy level for any three elements."
        },
        {
